Algorithm

1.Set low = 0 and high = n-1.
2.Find middle:
3.mid = (low + high)/2
4.If A[mid] == x, return the position.
5.If x < A[mid], search the left half.
6.Otherwise search the right half.
7.Repeat until low > high.

Complexity
Binary Search:

T(n)=T(n/2)+c
Therefore,
T(n)=O(log₂ n)  

Ternary Search:

T(n)=T(n/3)+c
Therefore,
T(n)=O(log₃ n)
Although log₃ n is mathematically smaller than log₂ n, ternary search performs more comparisons at every iteration because it checks two middle elements.

For example:
| Search  | Parts | Comparisons/iteration |
| ------- | ----: | --------------------: |
| Binary  |     2 |                     1 |
| Ternary |     3 |               up to 2 |
